  "body": "Apparently `TouchEvent` is always exposed in Chrome, but `document.createEvent(\"touchevent\")` depends on the \"touch events flag\" (see https://github.com/w3c/touch-events/issues/64). Having said that, neither Firefox nor Safari expose `TouchEvent` so maybe Chrome should change?\r\n\r\ncc @patrickhlauke @RByers \r\n\r\n(Firefox bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1693172.)",
